## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical concurrency on bare-metal MCUs: interrupt-safe data sharing, wrap-around handling, and overflow behavior in a tight, deterministic path.

## Key Concepts
- Circular buffers with power-of-two sizing
- Volatile indices and memory visibility between ISR and main code
- Minimal interrupt masking to avoid latency spikes
- Edge-case testing for wrap and overflow

## Code Example
```c
#define N 32
#define MASK (N-1)
static uint8_t buf[N];
static volatile uint8_t head = 0; // consumer index
static volatile uint8_t tail = 0; // producer index

int enqueue_byte(uint8_t b) {
  uint8_t next = (tail + 1) & MASK;
  if (next == head) return -1; // full
  buf[tail] = b;
  // memory barrier if available
  tail = next;
  return 0;
}

int dequeue_byte(uint8_t *out) {
  if (head == tail) return -1; // empty
  *out = buf[head];
  head = (head + 1) & MASK;
  return 0;
}
```

